A||N||5||Haze_Performance||Need turn signal/wiper help ||||8||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||02-03-2001||11:52 PM||||<B>This was the problem:<P>This started a few months ago when I removed my turn signal stalk (Pulled it out of the column). Well I tried to slide it back in but it wouldn't snap back in. (The slots were lined up) Well I pushed to hard and the switch must of broke. Now the left indicator comes on & stays on when I turn the lights on. (The left turn signal doesn't work at all now. Right works fine) Also the wipers will turn on & off for no reason while I'm driving. (Not only when I hit bumps)........<BR>(NONE OF THIS WAS HAPPENING BEFORE I MESSED WITH THE STALK)<P>This is what I did:<P>I picked up a good replacement wiper switch, turn signal switch & stalk from mrfiero. (I installed them today) I'm still having the same problem. It didn't help at all. I also checked all bulbs, fuses & connections. What can the problem be?<P>Can someone PLEASE give me an idea of what can be worng??? I hate the thought of going to the boneyard and buying a whole column for another $40.00.. And Im not sure if that will even solve the problem...<P>Thank You<BR>Carl  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> </B><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!!!!!!!!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!!!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 02-03-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||02-04-2001||06:37 AM||||"T" to the "O" to the "P"<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>WS6 Fieros "Members Photo Page"</A>||||reg||7
Z||000002||Greg Piet||02-04-2001||09:02 AM||||First for clarity...<BR>turn signal light is on with headlights...<BR>Does it flash?<BR>or is it the indicator light only that is illuminated?<P>the only thing that is popping to my mind is a pinched set of wires up there.<P>You may have already, or want to try this.<BR>Unplug the turn signal/stop light fuses, and turn on the headlights.  if the turn signal light is on you know it is getting power from somewhere else than it is supposed to be (most likely from the headlight wire).<BR>Dont remember what the Fiero uses, but likely an automatic resettable circuit breaker for the headlights(ANYONE?????)...  unplug that next.... if the turn signal light is still on you know at least which wire is the source.  Then it is just looking for where in the wire/switches it is bleeding to the turn signal.<P><BR>------------------<BR>SCCA Region 72<BR>#47 CSP<BR>Bring it to the track.<BR>Lets see if all those mods really helped!<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 02-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||02-04-2001||09:05 AM||||Oh yeah a GM service manual may help as well then you can test the pins of the stalk very easily to make sure they are peachy.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||02-04-2001||09:16 AM||||Haze,<P>Sounds like when you replaced the stalk the switch was damaged. The switch itself is located inside the steering column.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bob Englert||02-04-2001||09:20 AM||||The wiper switch inside the column can be gotten from Advance Auto or PartsAmerica.com.  It is GP Sorensen #DS170, should run around $55 or so.  You nned to remove the steering wheel, lock plate, and ignition key tmbler to get to and replace the wiper switch.  The turn signal switch is mounted at the same location, it might be worth replacing both while you are in there.<P>Tedious to do the first time, much easier the next time.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
